    "youtube_title": "Jewelry render basics: carat weight versus size",
    "caption": "A carat measures weight, not size. One carat is 200 milligrams, or a fifth of a gram, and a round diamond of one carat measures about 6.4 millimeters. Double the weight makes it only about a quarter wider. A denser stone, like sapphire, looks smaller at the same carat weight, while ovals and pears often look larger per carat than round stones. A deep cut hides weight below the girdle. Total carat weight adds up every diamond in a piece, and karat with a K is gold purity, not gem weight. So two stones of one carat can look quite different in size. A render shows a client how the design looks, before any stone is set.",
